Captain Sisay taps to fetch any legendary CARD — not just creatures. Lands, artifacts, enchantments, planeswalkers and even a sorcery are all on the table, so she is not a value engine, she is a toolbox that answers whatever the table is doing. Almost every game comes down to two questions: how fast can she untap, and do you know what to name.

# The commander, and untapping her
Captain Sisay :: {T}: search your library for a legendary card and put it in your HAND. Every activation is a card, so protecting her and untapping her is the whole game plan.
Lightning Greaves :: equip for zero, tap her the turn she lands, and shroud stops the removal spell aimed at her. This is the single best card to see alongside her.
Thousand-Year Elixir :: haste for the activation AND a repeatable untap. Two fetches a turn.
Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu :: the same haste clause, plus two mana specifically for creature abilities — and Sisay is a creature ability.
Seedborn Muse :: untaps everything on every opponent's untap step. Four Sisay activations per turn cycle, plus all your mana back to cast what she found.
Hall of the Bandit Lord :: the land that gives her haste on the turn you cast her, at the cost of three life.
Sigarda, Font of Blessings :: your OTHER permanents have hexproof, which includes Sisay. Fetch this the moment the table shows blue or black removal.
Avacyn, Angel of Hope :: your other permanents are indestructible. Between Avacyn and Sigarda, Sisay effectively cannot be answered.

# What to fetch, and when
Boseiju, Who Endures :: the answer nobody sees coming — Sisay fetches it as a LAND, and its channel destroys an artifact, enchantment or nonbasic land for less each legendary creature you control. Free interaction from a tutor.
Eiganjo, Seat of the Empire :: the same trick pointed at an attacker. Four damage, discounted by your board.
Talon Gates of Madara :: exiles a creature for four turns, again straight out of the mana base.
Gaea's Cradle :: the fetch that turns a board of legends into ten mana. Get it early, not late.
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: the other big-mana land. With Elesh Norn or Karametra on board it doubles your turn.
Plaza of Heroes :: fixes, protects a legend for {1} once, and it is fetchable.
Yavimaya Hollow :: regenerates the creature they just tried to kill.
Minas Tirith :: a card every turn you attacked with two creatures.
Linvala, Keeper of Silence :: turns off their mana dorks, sac outlets and activated-ability combos. The fetch against a combo table.
Thalia, Heretic Cathar :: everything of theirs enters tapped. The fetch against ramp and flash decks.
Grand Abolisher :: the fetch you name before you go for the kill turn.
Kutzil, Malamet Exemplar :: the second copy of that effect, and it draws off your pumped attackers.
Boromir, Warden of the Tower :: counters anything cast for no mana — Force of Will, Fierce Guardianship, Deflecting Swat, evoked Elementals. The fetch against a blue table.
Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite :: +2/+2 to your team and -2/-2 to theirs. Against a token deck it is a wrath; against anyone it is an anthem.
Urza's Ruinous Blast :: exiles every nonland permanent that is not legendary. Your board is legendary. This is a one-sided wrath you can tutor for, and it is why the deck plays so many legends over better nonlegendary cards.

# Making the legends cheap
Serah Farron :: the first legendary creature each turn costs {2} less, and it flips into a permanent +2/+2 anthem for your legends once you have three of them.
Radagast of Rhosgobel :: the first creature spell each turn costs {2} less and can be cast at instant speed. Fetch, then flash it in on their end step.
Gandalf the White :: legendary and artifact spells all gain flash, AND every legendary or artifact enters-or-leaves trigger happens twice. Loran destroys two things, Kogla fights twice, Solitude exiles two creatures.
Delighted Halfling :: taps for mana that legendary spells cannot be countered with. In a deck this legendary that is almost every spell.
Cavern of Souls :: name Human for Sisay herself, or whatever you are about to jam through a counterspell.
The Great Henge :: costs almost nothing with Ghalta or Kogla out, then it is two mana, two life, a counter and a card on every creature.

# Card advantage off being legendary
Reki, the History of Kamigawa :: a card for every legendary spell. In this deck he draws two or three a turn and costs three mana.
Venat, Heart of Hydaelyn :: the same trigger once a turn on a body that later exiles a permanent and flips into an indestructible engine.
Elena, Turk Recruit :: returns a legendary or artifact card from the graveyard on entry and grows on every historic spell.
Sylvan Library :: with this much tutoring you always know what the extra cards are worth paying for.
The One Ring :: protection from everything for a turn, then it draws an escalating pile. It is legendary, so Sisay finds it.
Loran of the Third Path :: destroys an artifact or enchantment on entry, twice with Gandalf, and taps for a symmetrical draw afterwards.
Eladamri, Korvecdal :: cast creatures off the top, and tap two creatures to put a creature straight onto the battlefield — which cheats past counterspells and mana entirely.
Selvala, Heart of the Wilds :: draws whenever anyone plays the biggest creature so far, and taps for mana equal to your largest creature. With Ghalta out that is twelve.

# Ramp
Birds of Paradise :: turn-one acceleration into a turn-three Sisay.
Avacyn's Pilgrim :: the white half of the same.
Llanowar Elves :: and the green half.
Arbor Elf :: untaps a Forest, which with Wild Growth or Utopia Sprawl on it is two or three mana.
Wild Growth :: the enchantment that makes Arbor Elf a Sol Ring.
Utopia Sprawl :: the same, and it fixes the white you need for the double-white cards.
Bloom Tender :: taps for both colours once Sisay is down.
Nature's Lore :: fetches Savannah or Canopy Vista untapped.
Three Visits :: the second copy.
Karametra, God of Harvests :: a land for every creature spell you cast, and an indestructible body once your devotion gets there.
Badgermole Cub :: every creature you tap for mana adds an extra green. With four dorks out that is four extra mana a turn.
Bugenhagen, Wise Elder :: fixes, and draws every upkeep once Ghalta or Kogla is on the battlefield.

# Removal and protection
Swords to Plowshares :: one mana, exiles anything.
Solitude :: free if you need it to be, and it exiles at instant speed. Gandalf makes it exile two.
Beast Within :: any permanent, at instant speed. The catch-all.
Generous Gift :: the white copy, so you can find both.
Austere Command :: pick the two halves that miss your own board. Against artifacts and small creatures it is a blowout.
Force of Vigor :: free on their turn, kills two artifacts or enchantments. The answer to a stax lock or a Rest in Peace.
Kogla, the Titan Ape :: fights on entry and destroys an artifact or enchantment every attack. Bounce a Human — Sisay is a Human — to save her from removal and give Kogla indestructible in the same breath.
Aven Mindcensor :: flash him onto their fetchland or tutor.
Flawless Maneuver :: free with a commander out. The answer to a wrath.
Heroic Intervention :: hexproof and indestructible for everything, including the lands Kamahl animated.
Veil of Summer :: one mana against blue and black, and it draws.
Legolas's Quick Reflexes :: split second, so nothing can respond. It saves a creature, untaps it, and turns it into a removal spell.
Spectacular Spider-Man :: flash blocker that sacrifices to give the whole board hexproof and indestructible.

# How you actually win
Akroma's Will :: with a commander out you take both halves. Flying, vigilance, double strike, lifelink, indestructible and protection from every colour on a board of pumped legends is lethal to the table, not just one player.
Kamahl, Heart of Krosa :: +3/+3 and trample every combat, forever, plus he animates your lands so the attack is wider than the board looks.
Ghalta, Stampede Tyrant :: costs almost nothing with a real board, and it empties your hand onto the battlefield when it lands.
Finale of Devastation :: for X of ten or more it is a tutor and a lethal team pump on the same card.
Surrak and Goreclaw :: trample for everything and a counter plus haste on every creature that enters — so the legends Sisay fetches attack the turn they arrive.
Flowering of the White Tree :: +2/+1 and ward {1} on the whole legendary board. The ward is what makes their spot removal stop working.
Sting, the Glinting Dagger :: haste and an untap each combat. On Sisay that is a free extra tutor every turn.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep any hand with a one-mana dork and three lands. Sisay on turn three, with haste or protection available on turn four, is the strongest start the deck has.
Do not fetch greedily. The first Sisay activation should usually be Lightning Greaves or Sigarda — something that keeps her alive — not the biggest legend in the library. A Sisay that survives two more turns finds four more cards.
Sisay's fetch puts the card in your HAND, so count the mana before you tap. Fetching an eight-drop you cannot cast is a wasted turn; fetching Boseiju or Eiganjo gives you a land drop AND a removal spell.
Urza's Ruinous Blast :: hold it. It is a legendary sorcery, so you need a legend already on board, and it exiles tokens, equipment and every nonlegendary creature at the table. Cast it when the pod has overcommitted, then attack into nothing.
